        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-24 13:54:15.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-6142 checkpatch: warn on GOTO() with a bare constant",
        "message": "LU-6142 checkpatch: warn on GOTO() with a bare constant\n\nGOTO() only logs its second argument, it never assigns it, so\nGOTO(label, -ENOMEM) reads like it sets the return value while\nactually discarding it and letting the target label return whatever\nwas there before. This turned out to be the common cause of several\nreal bugs, so warn about it at review time instead of finding the\nnext one the hard way. Existing occurrences are addressed separately.\n\nGOTO(label, rc), GOTO(label, rc = -ENOMEM) and GOTO(label, 0) stay\nsilent, and RETURN(), which does return its argument, is not matched.\nThe advice is worded conditionally because some matching sites are in\nfunctions with no rc to assign to. Only a plain constant is matched;\nthe same trap spelled as an expression is left for a follow-on, since\ncovering it multiplies the number of sites to triage.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8b0d2cf5b326b8445cacc7387110314427a732de\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
